    <h1>Full Assessment Detail (Appendix)</h1>
    <p class="note">Every question and response, including items that scored above the risk threshold.</p>
    <table class="report-table"><tr><th>Family</th><th>Question</th><th>Score</th><th>Notes</th></tr><tr><td>AC</td><td>Least-privilege access is enforced and reviewed for all OT user and service accounts.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>Remote vendor access through CyberArk with approval workflow; RBAC on the terminal SCADA.</td></tr><tr><td>AC</td><td>Role-based access control (RBAC) is implemented for HMI/SCADA and engineering workstation access.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>Remote vendor access through CyberArk with approval workflow; RBAC on the terminal SCADA.</td></tr><tr><td>AC</td><td>Remote and vendor access follows a documented, time-boxed, approved workflow (jump host / PAM).</td><td style="text-align:center;">4</td><td>Remote vendor access through CyberArk with approval workflow; RBAC on the terminal SCADA.</td></tr><tr><td>IA</td><td>Multi-factor authentication (MFA) is enforced for all remote and administrative OT access.</td><td style="text-align:center;">4</td><td>MFA on all remote access since 2025. Device certificates not used (Modbus/TCP only).</td></tr><tr><td>IA</td><td>Shared or generic OT accounts are minimized, with individual accountability where technically feasible.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>MFA on all remote access since 2025. Device certificates not used (Modbus/TCP only).</td></tr><tr><td>IA</td><td>Device and software identity (certificates, keys) is managed with a defined lifecycle (issuance, rotation, revocation).</td><td style="text-align:center;">2</td><td>MFA on all remote access since 2025. Device certificates not used (Modbus/TCP only).</td></tr><tr><td>SC</td><td>OT is segmented from the enterprise IT network via a dedicated industrial DMZ, with no direct session traversal permitted.</td><td style="text-align:center;">4</td><td>Industrial DMZ in place; conduit rules reviewed annually. No SIS at this site (SC Q3 marked N/A).</td></tr><tr><td>SC</td><td>Inter-zone conduits use default-deny, explicit allow-list firewall rules rather than broad 'any-any' access.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>Industrial DMZ in place; conduit rules reviewed annually. No SIS at this site (SC Q3 marked N/A).</td></tr><tr><td>SC</td><td>Safety Instrumented Systems (SIS), where present, are segmented as their own zone independent of the basic control system.</td><td style="text-align:center;">N/A</td><td>Industrial DMZ in place; conduit rules reviewed annually. No SIS at this site (SC Q3 marked N/A).</td></tr><tr><td>SI</td><td>Control logic and configuration changes are protected against unauthorized modification (integrity monitoring or equivalent).</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>SI</td><td>Firmware updates are verified against vendor cryptographic signatures before deployment.</td><td style="text-align:center;">2</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>SI</td><td>Malware protection is deployed where technically feasible, with documented compensating controls where it is not (legacy Level 0/1 devices).</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>AU</td><td>OT network traffic is monitored passively (SPAN/TAP) at every zone conduit — not via inline/blocking-mode sensors.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>Passive monitoring sensor at the DMZ boundary only; alerts go to the corporate SOC with generic rules.</td></tr><tr><td>AU</td><td>OT-derived alerts are onboarded into a SIEM/SOC with OT-aware correlation logic, not generic IT rules.</td><td style="text-align:center;">2</td><td>Passive monitoring sensor at the DMZ boundary only; alerts go to the corporate SOC with generic rules.</td></tr><tr><td>AU</td><td>Protocol-aware detection (Modbus, DNP3, OPC-UA, EtherNet/IP, PROFINET function codes) is in place, not just IP/port-level visibility.</td><td style="text-align:center;">2</td><td>Passive monitoring sensor at the DMZ boundary only; alerts go to the corporate SOC with generic rules.</td></tr><tr><td>IR</td><td>Containment decisions for OT incidents follow a documented, safety-reviewed process rather than automatic/unilateral isolation.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>Reporting obligations are handled by Legal after the fact, not built into the playbook.</td></tr><tr><td>IR</td><td>Pre-approved emergency isolation procedures exist and have been rehearsed for your highest-criticality zones.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>Reporting obligations are handled by Legal after the fact, not built into the playbook.</td></tr><tr><td>IR</td><td>Regulatory incident-reporting obligations (e.g., CISA, sector-specific) are built into the IR process as an explicit step.</td><td style="text-align:center;">2</td><td>Reporting obligations are handled by Legal after the fact, not built into the playbook.</td></tr><tr><td>CP</td><td>Verified 'golden image' backups (logic + configuration + firmware version) exist for your highest-criticality assets.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>CP</td><td>Restore capability is actually tested on a defined cadence, not merely assumed to work.</td><td style="text-align:center;">2</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>CP</td><td>Recovery Time/Point Objectives (RTO/RPO) are defined per asset criticality tier and approved by operations/safety.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>CM</td><td>Every change to a high-criticality OT asset passes through risk, safety, and security review gates before implementation.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>Asset inventory last reconciled 2024. No patch test environment.</td></tr><tr><td>CM</td><td>An accurate, current asset inventory is maintained and reconciled against engineering records at least annually.</td><td style="text-align:center;">3</td><td>Asset inventory last reconciled 2024. No patch test environment.</td></tr><tr><td>CM</td><td>Patches are validated in a representative staging environment before deployment to production Tier 1/2 assets.</td><td style="text-align:center;">2</td><td>Asset inventory last reconciled 2024. No patch test environment.</td></tr></table>

    
